  {
   "item_id": 14122601,
   "item_text": "3",
   "item_forum_id": 0,
   "item_type": "post",
   "in_feed": "0",
   "is_watched": "0",
   "item_score": "0",
   "id": "7858641",
   "item_level": "13",
   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 14122601,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 2013588,
    "poster_id": 363884,
    "post_rendered": "We call a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" > <i>interesting </i>if for each permutation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa35d9fc104207e09a712110ac81612c5b279a6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sigma$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" > of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/7/167ee76d3b20f5af5c140a0b439179db809f7e2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,\\ldots,n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" > there exist polynomials <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/1/1c1c76abf021bfef22bca1bab941229f85adafaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1,P_2,\\ldots ,P_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" > and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce56cfc237a035a5b060ddc685c710b3fa4af2e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\epsilon &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" > such that:<br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/6/f5655b34d3ed271b063522a7cbca0ff3865961e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"12\" height=\"18\" > <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/2/982375332cab67a6f2437d9527e4ac9c75c23d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1(0)=P_2(0)=\\ldots =P_n(0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"221\" height=\"18\" ><br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/0/e306d3df061bd255de2d15429decdf8192753b7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ii)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" > <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/4111a1e1dd1e8df84052bdf9897808a1db39ebae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1(x)&gt;P_2(x)&gt;\\ldots &gt;P_n(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"225\" height=\"18\" > for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/9/ee92c977c97b10e106bc73f8fc546371d6180406.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\epsilon&lt;x&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"89\" height=\"13\" ><br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/8/528d903396faf28af16a6a4340b29a3584acce19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$iii)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" > <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/c/9ac21d13c91b02395ce4b306272cd9c0ecefdc12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_{\\sigma (1)} (x)&gt;P_{\\sigma (2)}(x)&gt; \\ldots &gt;P_{\\sigma (n)} (x) $\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"280\" height=\"19\" > for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/4/5645cd0f3c00ea6efe885d99e1a01fa8d6379874.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;x&lt;\\epsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" ><br>\nFind all <i>interesting </i><span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\"  width=\"10\" height=\"8\" >.</span><br>\n<br>\n<i>Proposed by Mojtaba Zare Bidaki</i>",
    "post_canonical": "We call a number $n$ [i]interesting [/i]if for each permutation $\\sigma$ of $1,2,\\ldots,n$ there exist polynomials $P_1,P_2,\\ldots ,P_n$ and $\\epsilon > 0$ such that:\n$i)$ $P_1(0)=P_2(0)=\\ldots =P_n(0)$\n$ii)$ $P_1(x)>P_2(x)>\\ldots >P_n(x)$ for $-\\epsilon<x<0$\n$iii)$ $P_{\\sigma (1)} (x)>P_{\\sigma (2)}(x)> \\ldots >P_{\\sigma (n)} (x) $ for $0<x<\\epsilon$\nFind all [i]interesting [/i]$n$.\n\n[i]Proposed by Mojtaba Zare Bidaki[/i]",
    "username": "matinyousefi",
    "post_number": 1,
