   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 14282173,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 2028114,
    "poster_id": 224483,
    "post_rendered": "<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"11\" > is an odd prime number. Find all <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/3/c9378046b3bd8566b4d62f642a1480cfcf36aca2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{p-1}2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"42\" height=\"37\" >-</span>tuples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/c/cbce71175c2b1988495357345ec1b6882628920f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(x_1,x_2,\\dots,x_{\\frac{p-1}2}\\right)\\in \\mathbb{Z}_p^{\\frac{p-1}2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"198\" height=\"32\" > such that<br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/2/d329bb2b38258749664e5ba33a5013f80ef1bbfc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"$$\\sum_{i = 1}^{\\frac{p-1}{2}} x_{i} \\equiv \\sum_{i = 1}^{\\frac{p-1}{2}} x_{i}^{2} \\equiv \\cdots \\equiv \\sum_{i = 1}^{\\frac{p-1}{2}} x_{i}^{\\frac{p - 1}{2}} \\pmod p.$$\"  width=\"335\" height=\"56\" ><br>\n<i>Proposed by Ali Partofard</i>",
    "post_canonical": "$p$ is an odd prime number. Find all $\\frac{p-1}2$-tuples $\\left(x_1,x_2,\\dots,x_{\\frac{p-1}2}\\right)\\in \\mathbb{Z}_p^{\\frac{p-1}2}$ such that\n$$\\sum_{i = 1}^{\\frac{p-1}{2}} x_{i} \\equiv \\sum_{i = 1}^{\\frac{p-1}{2}} x_{i}^{2} \\equiv \\cdots \\equiv \\sum_{i = 1}^{\\frac{p-1}{2}} x_{i}^{\\frac{p - 1}{2}} \\pmod p.$$\n\n[i]Proposed by Ali Partofard[/i]",
